# Paths that enforce the project's limits need review by the boundary owners.
# Replace @your-org/boundary-owners with a real team or user that has write access,
# then put this block in CODEOWNERS, .github/CODEOWNERS or docs/CODEOWNERS.
# `boundaries codeowners --owner @team` prints the block for your project,
# including every path your manifests protect.

# BEGIN agent-terminus
/.boundaries/ @your-org/boundary-owners
/.claude/hooks/protect-boundaries.mjs @your-org/boundary-owners
/.claude/settings.json @your-org/boundary-owners
/.claude/settings.local.json @your-org/boundary-owners
/.githooks/pre-commit @your-org/boundary-owners
/.github/workflows/boundaries.yml @your-org/boundary-owners
/.github/CODEOWNERS @your-org/boundary-owners
/CODEOWNERS @your-org/boundary-owners
/docs/CODEOWNERS @your-org/boundary-owners
# Project boundary and safety tests, provider and probe files:
# add them to a manifest's [protected] paths, then regenerate this block with
# `boundaries codeowners --owner @your-org/boundary-owners`.
# /path/to/provider.py @your-org/boundary-owners
# END agent-terminus
